    "SolidCraft user report: resized hemisphere cut"
  ],
  "what": "A circumradius-50 regular hexagonal prism (z=0..50) is cut by a lower hemisphere of radius 69 centred at z = 72. The quarter-disc profile is split at radial distances 25 and 50. The radial-50 band meets the prism only at hex corners; no small circular tail is a distinct boundary. Expected roof z(r)=72-sqrt(69^2-r^2). The volume is the exact polar integral over six hexagonal wedges: V=(R+3)A-2*pi*R^3/3+4F, A=3*sqrt(3)*s^2/2, d=sqrt(3)*s/2, a=sqrt(R^2-d^2), b=sqrt(R^2-s^2), phi=asin(s/(2a)), F=R^3*atan(R/(sqrt(3)*b))-(3*a^2*d/2+d^3)*phi-d^2*b/(2*sqrt(3)), with s = 50 and R = 69. The hemisphere axis is shifted +5e-11 mm in X to exercise a distinct clipping event at an almost coincident corner. This changes the exact volume from the centred formula by at most A*delta*(50+delta)/sqrt(R^2-(50+delta)^2)<4e-7 mm^3, using the maximum derivative of the spherical roof. This bound is far below the grading tolerance; the positive shift is part of the input, not a boolean retry. Radius 69 reproduces status 1001 on SolidCraft commit f6d044089 at the reported radius offset 19.",
